{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YNS65sAi7jBwM5sgvEqdMq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a **personal productivity + R&D mission-control system** for J.C. Liechty. Grounded claims from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose â€” a single-folder GTD/task system.** It manages tasks, projects, and captured ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) entirely as plain markdown files in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” no database, no sync, markdown is the source of truth.\n\n- **What it ships â€” `anchor_gui.py`, the one declared deliverable.** A self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server (bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run as the persistent NSSM Windows service `anchor`) that generates an interactive browser dashboard and writes changes back to the markdown files. A CLI twin (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle + reliability.** Tasks move through active â†’ done â†’ cancelled/saved-for-later â†’ restored, each with optional notes. A daily 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) parses every file, exercises every endpoint on a throwaway port, walks a synthetic task through every state, and writes a dated health report â€” surfacing a red banner on failure.\n\n- **The bigger arc â€” an R&D \"Project Cockpit\" for trio-driven work.** Layered atop the task system (surfaces v2â†’v3â†’v4) is a control plane that turns each project into a single-screen cockpit for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio. Each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build) shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light; clicking expands an inline panel â€” a cached summary on top of a **real, resizable ConPTY terminal** below â€” where opening a session feels like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session (lane skill auto-loads once, greets once).\n\n- **Notable engineering commitments.** Strictly Python-stdlib **except one declared exception** â€” `pywinpty` for the optional ConPTY terminal subsystem (lazy import, `pty_manager.py` only, degrades gracefully if absent). Sessions get git-worktree isolation; deliverable previews run on OS-assigned ports hard-guarded `â‰  8777`; summaries are proactively generated, grounding-filtered, and cached. v4 (\"Project Cockpit\") is **built and merged to master** (commit `38fd70e`, 9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passing).\n\n- **Branding.** Presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\", using the vendored brand mark as favicon and masthead lockup."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a790072-682c-48fe-a114-a3fddfb70a1d","uuid":"577f57f8-e350-4c3f-b9f4-300fdad13d97","request_id":"req_011Cc1JbAAJCkWe61L7zDcqQ"}
